# Bluetooth (ADR 0113): slate-btd holds the host stack over /dev/hci0
# when a controller is there (it waits for one otherwise), keeps the
# pairings in /var/lib/slate/bluetooth, and answers Settings and slate-bt
# on the abstract socket slate-btd. slinit runs and supervises it.
### BEGIN INIT INFO
# Provides:          slate-btd
# Required-Start:
# Required-Stop:
# Should-Start:      logd devd
# Default-Start:     2 3 4 5
# Default-Stop:      0 1 6
# Short-Description: Bluetooth
# X-Slate-Exec:      /bin/slate-btd
### END INIT INFO
exit 0
